@startuml Sequence_Coordinator_Crash_Resume
autonumber
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial

participant Coordinator as "Coordinator State Machine"
database DB as "PostgreSQL"
folder Storage as "File Storage"
actor Admin as "System / Administrator"

== Regular Execution with State Persistence ==
Note over Coordinator, DB
  Coordinator saves state after EVERY transition:
  - run_id, active_round_id, status (COLLECTING/AGGREGATING)
  - latest global model version and path
end note
Coordinator -> DB : UPDATE rounds SET status='AGGREGATING' WHERE round_id=5
Coordinator -> Storage : Write global_model_v6.safetensors
Coordinator -> DB : UPDATE rounds SET status='COMPLETED' WHERE round_id=5
Coordinator -> DB : UPDATE runs SET current_round=6 WHERE run_id='run-101'

== Unexpected Crash ==
Note over Coordinator : [CRASH: Power failure / Process killed / OOM]

== Recovery & Resume ==
Admin -> Coordinator : Start Coordinator process (Restart / systemd)
Coordinator -> DB : SELECT * FROM runs WHERE status='IN_PROGRESS'
DB --> Coordinator : run_id='run-101', current_round=6
Coordinator -> DB : SELECT * FROM rounds WHERE run_id='run-101' ORDER BY round_id DESC LIMIT 1
DB --> Coordinator : round_id=5 (status='COMPLETED'), model_version=6

Coordinator -> Storage : Verify global_model_v6.safetensors exists & checksum matches
Storage --> Coordinator : File Verified OK

Coordinator -> DB : Log Event: "COORDINATOR_RESUMED" (resuming from round 6)
Coordinator -> Coordinator : Initialize Round 6 (State: OPEN)
Note over Coordinator : Round 6 begins seamlessly.\nClients polling /task now receive round 6 without starting from round 0!
@enduml
